IOP modules for mmcefs
======================

mmcefs loads these into the IOP on its first mount if they are not already
running.  Install them on the PS2 root filesystem:

  mkdir -p /lib/modules/irx
  cp iomanX.irx fileXio.irx mmceman.irx /lib/modules/irx/

(or point the module parameter irx_dir= at another directory).

  file          source                                         sha256
  iomanX.irx    ps2sdk v2.0.0 + PSBBN compat, no-op shutdown   b38759959baf67f15a2651d80f562c89e14fea688034006ef536b9e3e218009d
  fileXio.irx   ps2sdk, ps2dev release v2.0.0 (2026-05-17)     d158651ca5fcf623e12913a27d0ab1b7f94b03c9e700e7bcc223cf898a7e6711
  mmceman.irx   ps2-mmce/mmceman + PSBBN/SIO2/VFS fixes        d60b73eb85910869e9b97061ed4c45094f18c9e96574390707f214b6fedbc247
  poweroff.irx  ps2sdk v2.0.0                                  2de34ce2aa4f2f65d74594c27282ccf036083b49dd8a167849dbba3c7ba1ad5d

iomanX.irx and fileXio.irx are part of ps2sdk (https://github.com/ps2dev/ps2sdk),
licensed under the Academic Free License 2.0 (LICENSE.ps2sdk).
mmceman.irx is by the MMCE authors (https://github.com/ps2-mmce/mmceman),
licensed under the MIT license (LICENSE.mmceman).

iomanX.irx: shutdown() (export 2) is patched to return 1 without calling
unhook_ioman().  loadcore calls it when the IOP reboots, and unhook_ioman()
calls deinit() on every device, including the ones taken over from the
original IOMAN.  The IOP then never finished rebooting, so native programs
started through akmem (BootNative, the __mbr osdboot) hung.
